diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e382ce22d7e2eb8eb07c4a4eb37a82e053bfffa7..06441d7c2e909884ff2ebfc776c82ca7ffc7fd01 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -32,7 +32,12 @@ day or more that does not start and end at midnight UTC, and an hourly rental of
 Booking also throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period.
 
 Periods are half-open, so a booking ending on 3 July does not block one starting on 3 July, and a booking ending
-at 12:00 does not block one starting at 12:00. Cancellations are not implemented yet; the cancellation policy
-will be added later.
+at 12:00 does not block one starting at 12:00.
+
+`cancel(bookingId, at)` cancels a booking at the whole hour `at` (UTC) and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`. A
+cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, so `availability` and `book` treat its period as free again. A
+booking can only be cancelled once: cancelling it again throws, and so does an unknown booking id. The refund is
+the whole amount the booking cost, because the cancellation policy is not set yet; once it is, the refund will
+depend on when the booking is cancelled, which is why `at` is taken.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
